  Flags, in the game's order (scenario.json.erb:240 targetFlags, :1343 station):
    flag_1 flag{network_scan_complete}    - - service banners: FTP login banner + web index source
    flag_2 flag{ftp_intel_gathered}       - - ProFTPD 1.3.3c source backdoor -> root
    flag_3 flag{pricing_intel_decoded}    - - ROT13 price list on the web host, decode
    flag_4 flag{distcc_legacy_compromised}- - distcc_exec (CVE-2004-2687, 3632) -> logs

  Exactly FOUR flag generators. The round-1 draft had five (flag1 generated twice:
  once in the FTP anonymous pre-leak, once in the web index), which would have given
  the station five flags and shifted flagRewards[3] (the transaction log) onto the
  wrong flag. flag1 is now generated once, into the scan_flag datastore, and the same
  value is shown in both banners.

  CAVEATs (for the user):
   - flag1: nmap alone emits no flag. It sits in what the services say about
     themselves: the FTP login banner (welcome_msg -> AccessGrantMsg, shown on an
     anonymous login) and an HTML comment in the web host's index page. This matches
     the task text "read the service banners the scan turns up" (scenario.json.erb:238).
     It is NOT in the anonymous FTP folder: the in-game runbook says "nothing that
     matters lives in the anonymous folder" (scenario.json.erb:1274).
   - Flag order assumes SecGen generates the system-level scan_flag datastore before
     the module inputs (as m02's system-level account datastore is). Confirm on a
     test build that flags_by_vm comes back in the order above.
   - The game's "training network" is modelled here as ONE multi-service target box
     (FTP + web + distcc). A multi-host build is possible but heavier; one box honours
     "map the network" because the scan still finds three services to enumerate.
   - Price list (flag 3) is the PUBLIC version of lore_fragment_2 (scenario.json.erb:57):
     same tiers, prices and healthcare-premium note under a CONFIDENTIAL filing line
     (HaX: "they filed it as confidential"), but no buyer names, no SOLD ledger and no
     reserved Phase 2 stock (design review P3-2, 2026-10-04). Those stay in the game's
     wall-safe catalogue, so cracking the safe pays out something the VM doesn't.
   - Transaction log (flag 4) is operational_log_content verbatim (scenario.json.erb:61),
